      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "READ ME",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "🎨 This workflow uses the Qwen 2511 Image Edit node to merge elements from three separate images into one cohesive piece.\n________________________________________________________________________\n\n1. 📥 The Core Setup\nImage 1: Acts as your base composition.\n\nImage 2: Provides specific subjects (e.g., characters, objects).\n\nImage 3: Provides environmental details (e.g., backgrounds, lighting).\n________________________________________________________________________\n2. ✍️ Prompting Strategy\nUse a \"Director’s Prompt\" to tell the node exactly what to do with each input. Reference them by name:\n\n\"Replace the people in image_1 with the aliens from image_2, and use the background from image_3.\"\n________________________________________________________________________\n3. ⚙️ Tuning Parameters\nFor best results, manage your settings with precision:\n\n\nSeed: Keep this Fixed while refining your prompt. Change it only when you are ready to explore different creative variations of the same composition.\n\nShift: * Low values: Enhance fine, technical details.\n\nHigh values: Manage larger, structural changes.\n\nSteps & CFG: These are generally pre-optimized for the model's Lora.\n\nSteps: Keep at 8 unless you require more refinement.\n\nCFG: Maintain at 1.0 to prevent color distortion and keep the edit grounded in your source images.\n________________________________________________________________________\n💡 Artist TipAlways keep your Seed fixed while tweaking the prompt text. This ensures that any changes you see are the result of your words, not random noise."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
